 "amendment_1": "2026-11-02, made after seeing that all three Model B v2 seeds selected tau=0.10, the lower edge of the 0.10-0.70 grid: the grid was extended downward (0.01, 0.02, 0.03, 0.05, 0.07) for the Model B arms only, re-running the same checkpoints on the same cached calibration frames at a detector floor of 0.01 (eval/level3_boundary_check.py), and the SAME rule (argmax F0.5, ties to the higher tau) was applied. Calibration scenarios only; no pilot or held-out result was used. Model A arms were interior optima (0.45/0.30/0.35) and are unchanged. B2s0 and B2s1 select 0.01, the practical floor of the detector, so for them the optimum is still at the grid edge: their confidences on synthetic smoke are very low, and lower is not testable."
